          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Jean-Paul Sartre</strong><br>\nJean-Paul Sartre was a French existentialist philosopher, playwright, novelist, political activist, biographer, and literary critic. He was born on June 21, 1905, in Paris, France. Sartre is known for his leading role in the 20th-century existentialist movement, which emphasizes the individual's freedom and responsibility to give meaning to life. Despite losing his father at a young age, Sartre excelled in his studies, particularly at the École Normale Supérieure, where he studied philosophy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Early Influences</strong><br>\nSartre's early works were influenced by German philosopher Edmund Husserl's phenomenology, which studies the structures of consciousness as experienced from a first-person perspective. During his time as a student, Sartre was also greatly influenced by the writings of Heidegger and Kierkegaard. He later became a professor of philosophy at Le Havre, where he began to develop his existentialist ideas.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Existentialism and Freedom</strong><br>\nSartre's philosophy centers on the concept of existential freedom. He believed that people are \"condemned to be free,\" meaning that with no predetermined essence, individuals must create their own essence through actions. His existentialist motto, \"existence precedes essence,\" suggests that humans exist first and then define their purpose, contrasting with traditional philosophical views that essence or nature comes first.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
